.TH CJSON_SERIALIZE_PRETTY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cjson_serialize_pretty \- serialize a DOM tree to an indented JSON string
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cjson.h>

char *cjson_serialize_pretty(cjson node, unsigned int indent);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Works like cjson_serialize(), but writes newlines and indents each
nesting level with spaces.  An indent of 0 selects the default of 4
spaces, so for compact output with no indent you use
cjson_serialize() instead.  Object members come out in the same
insertion order as with cjson_serialize(3).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A null-terminated string on the heap, from the root node's allocator.
Free it the same way as the result of cjson_serialize(3): with
cjson_serialize_free() when the tree uses the default allocator, and
with cjson_serialize_free_mp() when it uses a custom one.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cjson_dictionary_first (3),
.BR cjson_serialize (3)
